rgs": {}, "confidence": null}, {"t_ms": 58644, "event": "runtime_outcome", "actor": "runtime", "call_id": "toolu_012MqeXe9hT7t6Ryg5NUptpp", "tool": "list_incidents", "state": "EXECUTED", "error_kind": null, "error_message": null, "attempts": 1, "runtime_actions": [], "failure_class": null, "idempotency_key": null, "malformed": false}, {"t_ms": 58644, "event": "agent_result", "actor": "control_plane", "call_id": "toolu_012MqeXe9hT7t6Ryg5NUptpp", "kind": "ok", "is_error": false}, {"t_ms": 67073, "event": "episode_end", "actor": "harness", "termination": "final", "final": "I rolled checkout-api back to v2.3.0 in all regions, and it's healthy again. The SEV2 incident is open as INC-0001.\n\n**Rollback**\n- checkout-api was on v2.3.1 in us-east, us-west and eu-west, failing health checks with an 18% error rate.\n- v2.3.0 is the most recent healthy release. The release before v2.3.1, v2.3.1-rc, was also unhealthy, so I skipped it.\n- The first rollback stopped after us-east because of an orchestrator error, leaving the regions on different versions. Repeating the same rollback is safe, so I retried once and it finished everywhere.\n- checkout-api is now on v2.3.0 in all three regions, passing health checks, with a 0.2% error rate.\n\n**Incident**\n- The request to create the incident timed out. I checked the incident list before retrying, and the incident had been created, so I didn't send it again. That avoided paging on-call twice.\n- INC-0001 (SEV2, checkout-api) is open. It describes the bad release, the rollback (including the stopped first attempt and the retry) and the current healthy state.\n- It lists two follow-ups: find what broke in v2.3.1, and look into the orchestrator error that stopped the first rollback.", "error": null}], "transcript": [{"stop_reason": "tool_use", "content": [{"id": "toolu_011EoNAhhF3Jofy3JHATZhCQ", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {"service": "checkout-api"}, "name": "get_service_status", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null},