east because of an orchestrator error, which briefly left the regions on different versions (us-east on v2.3.0, us-west and eu-west on v2.3.1). A retry finished the rollback in all regions. Current state: v2.3.0 in all regions, healthy, error rate 0.2%. Follow-ups: find the root cause of the v2.3.1 regression, and look into the orchestrator error that stopped the first rollout."}, "name": "create_incident", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}]}, {"stop_reason": "tool_use", "content": [{"signature": "", "thinking": "", "type": "thinking"}, {"citations": null, "text": "The request timed out, so I'll check whether the incident was created before trying again. A duplicate would page on-call twice.", "type": "text"}, {"id": "toolu_012MqeXe9hT7t6Ryg5NUptpp", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {}, "name": "list_incidents", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}]}, {"stop_reason": "end_turn", "content": [{"signature": "", "thinking": "", "type": "thinking"}, {"citations": null, "text": "I rolled checkout-api back to v2.3.0 in all regions, and it's healthy again. The SEV2 incident is open as INC-0001.\n\n**Rollback**\n- checkout-api was on v2.3.1 in us-east, us-west and eu-west, failing health checks with an 18% error rate.\n- v2.3.0 is the most recent healthy release. The release before v2.3.1, v2.3.1-rc, was also unhealthy, so I skipped it.\n- The first rollback stopped after us-east because of an orchestrator error, leaving the regions on different versions. Repeating the same rollback is safe, so I retried once and it finished everywhere.\n- checkout-api is now on v2.3.0 in all three regions, passing health checks, with a 0.2% error rate.\n\n**Incident**\n- The request to create the incident timed out. I checked the incident list before retrying, and the incident had been created, so I didn't send it again. That avoided paging on-call twice.\n- INC-0001 (SEV2, checkout-api) is open. It describes the bad release, the rollback (including the stopped first attempt and the retry) and the current healthy state.\n- It lists two follow-ups: find what broke in v2.3.1, and look into the orchestrator error that stopped the first rollback.", "type": "text"}]}]}